From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: keep a clipped Blt's clip rects to the destination surface

Wine does not clip a window's visible region to the screen, so the clip list of a window clipper
for a window partly off the screen reaches past the primary surface, and ddraw_surface_blt_clipped
blitted those rects as they were: the Blt failed with DDERR_INVALIDRECT and drew nothing. Wine's
VMR-7 blits every video frame to the primary through a clipper on its video window, so a window
the film's own size (1280x720 plus its frame, wider than a 1280 screen) stayed blank: in
GraphStudioNext the "ActiveMovie Window" was white while the sound played ("Failed to blit, hr
0x88760096" per frame). Windows never draws outside the surface: each clip rect is now kept to the
destination surface, the source rect following, and a rect wholly outside is skipped.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
--- a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
@@ -1792,7 +1792,7 @@
 {
     RECT src_rect, dst_rect;
     float scale_x, scale_y;
-    const RECT *clip_rect;
+    RECT *clip_rect;
     DWORD clip_list_size;
     RGNDATA *clip_list;
     HRESULT hr = DD_OK;
@@ -1870,6 +1870,22 @@
     {
         RECT src_rect_clipped = src_rect;
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DDRAW_CLIP_PAST_SURFACE
+        /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 8408): a window's visible region is not clipped to the screen
+         * in Wine, so the clip list of a window partly off the screen reaches past the primary
+         * surface, and blitting that rect failed with DDERR_INVALIDRECT: nothing was drawn. The
+         * VMR-7 blits every frame this way, so a video window the film's own size (1280x720 in
+         * its frame is wider than a 1280 screen) stayed blank (GraphStudioNext). Windows never
+         * draws outside the surface: keep each clip rect to it and the source to match. */
+        {
+            RECT bounds;
+
+            SetRect(&bounds, 0, 0, dst_surface->surface_desc.dwWidth, dst_surface->surface_desc.dwHeight);
+            if (!IntersectRect(&clip_rect[i], &clip_rect[i], &bounds))
+                continue;
+        }
+#endif
+
         if (src_surface)
         {
             src_rect_clipped.left += (LONG)((clip_rect[i].left - dst_rect.left) * scale_x);
